---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import PageBody from "../components/PageBody.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Code from "../components/Code.astro";
import OptionsTable from "../components/api/OptionsTable.astro";
import { defineSections } from "../lib/sections";

const S = defineSections([
  { id: "anatomy", label: "Anatomy", heading: false },
  { id: "dial-pad", label: "Dial pad" },
  { id: "keyboard", label: "Keyboard" },
  { id: "keys", label: "Keys" },
  { id: "accessibility", label: "Accessibility" },
  { id: "tokens", label: "Tokens" },
  { id: "options", label: "Options" },
  { id: "methods", label: "Methods" },
]);

const digits = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9];
const dial = [["1", ""], ["2", "ABC"], ["3", "DEF"], ["4", "GHI"], ["5", "JKL"], ["6", "MNO"], ["7", "PQRS"], ["8", "TUV"], ["9", "WXYZ"], ["*", ""], ["0", "+"], ["#", ""]];
const rows = ["qwertyuiop", "asdfghjkl", "zxcvbnm"];
---
<DocsLayout page="keypad">
<PageBody sections={S}>
  <Section {...S.anatomy}>
        <p class="flow-text">
          A keypad or keyboard is a set of on-screen keys that type into a text field.
        </p>
        <p>
          A <code>.keypad</code> is three columns of round keys for PINs,
          codes and amounts. A <code>.keyboard</code> is rows of keys for
          text. Both are a <code>role="group"</code> with a name, and
          <code>aria-controls</code> names the field they type into. Every key
          is a <code>&lt;button type="button"&gt;</code>. A key with a
          <code>value</code> types it at the caret, and the field gets the
          same <code>input</code> event typing would fire.
          <code>AutoInit()</code> starts every <code>.keypad</code> and
          <code>.keyboard</code>.
        </p>
        <div data-markdown-ignore style="display: grid; gap: 16px; justify-items: center">
          <div class="field outlined">
            <input id="demo-pin" type="password" inputmode="none" maxlength="6" placeholder=" " autocomplete="off">
            <label for="demo-pin">PIN</label>
          </div>
          <div class="keypad" role="group" aria-label="PIN keypad" aria-controls="demo-pin">
            {digits.map((d) => <button type="button" value={String(d)}>{d}</button>)}
            <span></span>
            <button type="button" value="0">0</button>
            <button type="button" data-key="Backspace" aria-label="Delete"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">backspace</span></button>
          </div>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<div class="field outlined">
  <input id="pin" type="password" inputmode="none" maxlength="6" placeholder=" " autocomplete="off">
  <label for="pin">PIN</label>
</div>

<div class="keypad" role="group" aria-label="PIN keypad" aria-controls="pin">
  <button type="button" value="1">1</button>
  <button type="button" value="2">2</button>
  <!-- … 3 to 9 … -->
  <span></span>
  <button type="button" value="0">0</button>
  <button type="button" data-key="Backspace" aria-label="Delete">
    <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">backspace</span>
  </button>
</div>
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S["dial-pad"]}>
        <p>
          Put a key's letters in a <code>&lt;small&gt;</code> after the digit.
          A key with a button style class keeps that style, so a call key is
          a <code>filled</code> button. Add <code>wide</code> to a key to span
          two cells as a pill, which fills the last row beside Backspace.
        </p>
        <div data-markdown-ignore style="display: grid; gap: 16px; justify-items: center">
          <div class="field">
            <input id="demo-phone" type="tel" inputmode="none" placeholder=" " autocomplete="off">
            <label for="demo-phone">Phone number</label>
          </div>
          <div class="keypad" role="group" aria-label="Dial pad" aria-controls="demo-phone">
            {dial.map(([d, l]) => <button type="button" value={d}>{d}{l && <small aria-hidden="true">{l}</small>}</button>)}
            <button type="button" class="filled wide" data-key="Enter" aria-label="Call"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">call</span></button>
            <button type="button" data-key="Backspace" aria-label="Delete"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">backspace</span></button>
          </div>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<div class="keypad" role="group" aria-label="Dial pad" aria-controls="phone">
  <button type="button" value="2">2<small aria-hidden="true">ABC</small></button>
  <!-- … -->
  <button type="button" class="filled wide" data-key="Enter" aria-label="Call">
    <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">call</span>
  </button>
  <button type="button" data-key="Backspace" aria-label="Delete">
    <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">backspace</span>
  </button>
</div>
`} />
        <h3>Backspace in the field</h3>
        <p>
          For a centered call key, move Backspace into the text field as a
          trailing <code>icon-button suffix</code> and hold the cells beside
          the call key open with empty <code>&lt;span&gt;</code> elements. A
          <code>data-key</code> key inside the field's <code>.field</code> works
          like a keypad key, even when the field renders after the keypad.
          Other buttons there, such as a password toggle, keep their own behavior.
        </p>
        <div data-markdown-ignore style="display: grid; gap: 16px; justify-items: center">
          <div class="field">
            <input id="demo-phone-b" type="tel" inputmode="none" placeholder=" " autocomplete="off">
            <label for="demo-phone-b">Phone number</label>
            <button type="button" class="icon-button suffix" data-key="Backspace" aria-label="Delete"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">backspace</span></button>
          </div>
          <div class="keypad" role="group" aria-label="Dial pad, Backspace in the field" aria-controls="demo-phone-b">
            {dial.map(([d, l]) => <button type="button" value={d}>{d}{l && <small aria-hidden="true">{l}</small>}</button>)}
            <span></span>
            <button type="button" class="filled" data-key="Enter" aria-label="Call"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">call</span></button>
            <span></span>
          </div>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<div class="field">
  <input id="phone" type="tel" inputmode="none" placeholder=" " autocomplete="off">
  <label for="phone">Phone number</label>
  <button type="button" class="icon-button suffix" data-key="Backspace" aria-label="Delete">
    <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">backspace</span>
  </button>
</div>

<div class="keypad" role="group" aria-label="Dial pad" aria-controls="phone">
  <!-- 1 to # -->
  <span></span>
  <button type="button" class="filled" data-key="Enter" aria-label="Call">
    <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">call</span>
  </button>
  <span></span>
</div>
`} />
        <h3>A third action</h3>
        <p>
          A key with a <code>data-key</code> the script does not know types
          nothing and calls <code>onKey</code> with its name, so the empty cell
          can hold a page action such as contacts.
        </p>
        <div data-markdown-ignore style="display: grid; gap: 16px; justify-items: center">
          <div class="field">
            <input id="demo-phone-c" type="tel" inputmode="none" placeholder=" " autocomplete="off">
            <label for="demo-phone-c">Phone number</label>
          </div>
          <div class="keypad" role="group" aria-label="Dial pad with contacts" aria-controls="demo-phone-c">
            {dial.map(([d, l]) => <button type="button" value={d}>{d}{l && <small aria-hidden="true">{l}</small>}</button>)}
            <button type="button" data-key="Contacts" aria-label="Contacts"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">contacts</span></button>
            <button type="button" class="filled" data-key="Enter" aria-label="Call"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">call</span></button>
            <button type="button" data-key="Backspace" aria-label="Delete"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">backspace</span></button>
          </div>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<div class="keypad" role="group" aria-label="Dial pad" aria-controls="phone">
  <!-- 1 to # -->
  <button type="button" data-key="Contacts" aria-label="Contacts">
    <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">contacts</span>
  </button>
  <button type="button" class="filled" data-key="Enter" aria-label="Call">
    <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">call</span>
  </button>
  <button type="button" data-key="Backspace" aria-label="Delete">
    <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">backspace</span>
  </button>
</div>

<script>
Expressive.Keypad.init(document.querySelector('.keypad'), {
  onKey: (key) => { if (key === 'Contacts') openContacts(); },
});
</script>
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.keyboard}>
        <p>
          Each child of a <code>.keyboard</code> is a row. A character key is
          a tenth of the row and may shrink, a function key is one and a half
          keys wide, and the space bar takes what is left. A nine-key row is
          centered, which gives QWERTY its half-key indent. Set
          <code>--md-comp-keyboard-columns</code> for a layout with more or
          fewer keys in its widest row.
        </p>
        <p>
          An optional <code>&lt;div class="numbers"&gt;</code> row of digits
          sits above the letters with shorter 40dp keys. Leave it out, or add
          <code>hidden</code> to drop it and remove <code>hidden</code> to show
          it again.
        </p>
        <div data-markdown-ignore style="display: grid; gap: 16px">
          <div class="field">
            <textarea id="demo-note" inputmode="none" placeholder=" "></textarea>
            <label for="demo-note">Message</label>
          </div>
          <label class="switch">
            <input type="checkbox" id="demo-number-row" checked>
            Number row
          </label>
          <div class="keyboard" role="group" aria-label="Keyboard" aria-controls="demo-note">
            <div class="numbers" id="demo-numbers">{[..."1234567890"].map((c) => <button type="button" value={c}>{c}</button>)}</div>
            {rows.slice(0, 2).map((row) => <div>{[...row].map((c) => <button type="button" value={c}>{c}</button>)}</div>)}
            <div>
              <button type="button" data-key="Shift" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Shift"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">shift</span></button>
              {[...rows[2]].map((c) => <button type="button" value={c}>{c}</button>)}
              <button type="button" data-key="Backspace" aria-label="Delete"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">backspace</span></button>
            </div>
            <div>
              <button type="button" value=",">,</button>
              <button type="button" value=" " aria-label="Space"></button>
              <button type="button" value=".">.</button>
              <button type="button" data-key="Enter" aria-label="New line"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">keyboard_return</span></button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<div class="keyboard" role="group" aria-label="Keyboard" aria-controls="message">
  <div class="numbers">
    <button type="button" value="1">1</button>
    <!-- … 2 to 0 … -->
  </div>
  <div>
    <button type="button" value="q">q</button>
    <!-- … w to p … -->
  </div>
  <div><!-- a to l --></div>
  <div>
    <button type="button" data-key="Shift" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Shift">
      <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">shift</span>
    </button>
    <!-- z to m -->
    <button type="button" data-key="Backspace" aria-label="Delete">
      <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">backspace</span>
    </button>
  </div>
  <div>
    <button type="button" value=",">,</button>
    <button type="button" value=" " aria-label="Space"></button>
    <button type="button" value=".">.</button>
    <button type="button" data-key="Enter" aria-label="New line">
      <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">keyboard_return</span>
    </button>
  </div>
</div>
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.keys}>
        <table class="striped">
          <thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>value="…"</code></td><td>Types the value at the caret, replacing any selection. Typing stops at the field's <code>maxlength</code>.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>data-key="Backspace"</code></td><td>Deletes the selection, or the character before the caret.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>data-key="Enter"</code></td><td>Submits the field's form with <code>requestSubmit()</code>, so validation runs. In a <code>&lt;textarea&gt;</code> it types a new line.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>data-key="Shift"</code></td><td>Toggles <code>aria-pressed</code>. While pressed the character keys show capitals, and the next one types a capital and releases Shift.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>data-key="CapsLock"</code></td><td>Toggles <code>aria-pressed</code>. While pressed the character keys show and type capitals, until it is pressed again.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>data-key="Layer"</code></td><td>Shows the elements in the keyboard whose <code>data-layer</code> matches the key's <code>value</code> and hides those with another <code>data-layer</code>, such as a row of symbols in place of the letters. Elements without <code>data-layer</code> always show.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Any other <code>data-key</code></td><td>Types nothing and calls <code>onKey</code> with its name.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>
          A <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> without <code>value</code> or
          <code>data-key</code> is not a key, so the script ignores it. Keys
          type at the caret; a field nobody has clicked into takes them at the
          end. While the field has focus, a hardware key held down presses the
          matching on-screen key, so the keyboard shows what is typed. Number
          and email inputs have no caret position to read, so keys
          type at the end. A number input empties itself on a partial value
          such as <code>12.</code> or <code>-</code>, so the key is ignored
          there. For decimals and signs, use a text field with
          <code>inputmode="none"</code>.
        </p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.accessibility}>
        <ul class="browser-default">
          <li>Name the group with <code>aria-label</code> and point <code>aria-controls</code> at the field. Give the field its own label.</li>
          <li>Give every key <code>type="button"</code>, or a key inside a form submits it. Name icon keys and the space bar with <code>aria-label</code>.</li>
          <li>Browsers check <code>minlength</code> only on what a person types, and a keypad's input comes from a script, so the keypad checks it: a shorter value gets the <code>i18n.tooShort</code> message until it is long enough. It never replaces a message the page set, and a form reset or <code>destroy()</code> clears its own. <code>pattern</code> and <code>required</code> apply as usual.</li>
          <li>Add <code>inputmode="none"</code> to the field so a phone or tablet keeps its own keyboard closed. A hardware keyboard still types into the field.</li>
          <li>A pointer press keeps focus and the caret in the field while it has focus. Keys stay native buttons, so Tab, Enter and Space reach them.</li>
          <li>Keys are 72dp on a keypad and 48dp tall on a keyboard. Keep a keyboard wide enough that a character key stays at least 24px wide.</li>
        </ul>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.tokens}>
        <table class="striped">
          <thead><tr><th>Token</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-keypad-key-size</code></td><td>72px</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-keypad-gap</code></td><td>12px</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-keypad-key-color</code></td><td><code>surface-container-highest</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-keypad-key-label-color</code></td><td><code>on-surface</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-keypad-function-key-color</code></td><td><code>secondary-container</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-keypad-function-key-label-color</code></td><td><code>on-secondary-container</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-keypad-key-pressed-shape</code></td><td>12px; keyboard: 6px</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-keyboard-columns</code></td><td>10</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-keyboard-gap</code></td><td>6px</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-keyboard-key-height</code></td><td>48px</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-keyboard-number-key-height</code></td><td>40px</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-keyboard-key-shape</code></td><td>12px</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-keyboard-container-color</code></td><td><code>surface-container</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-keyboard-container-shape</code></td><td>16px</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.options}>
        <OptionsTable>
          <tr><td><code>onKey</code></td><td>Function</td><td><code>null</code></td><td>Called after every key press with the text typed (<code>'7'</code>, <code>'A'</code>, <code>' '</code>) or the function key's name (<code>'Backspace'</code>, <code>'Enter'</code>, <code>'Shift'</code>, <code>'CapsLock'</code>, <code>'Layer'</code>). Works without <code>aria-controls</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>i18n.tooShort</code></td><td>Function</td><td>English</td><td>Takes the field's <code>minlength</code> and returns the validation message for a shorter keypad-typed value: <code>Use at least 3 characters.</code></td></tr>
        </OptionsTable>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.methods}>
<Code code={`
const keypad = Expressive.Keypad.getInstance(el);
keypad.target;    // the field named by aria-controls, or null
keypad.destroy(); // removes the listeners
`} />
  </Section>
</PageBody>
<script is:inline>
document.getElementById('demo-number-row').addEventListener('change', (e) => {
  document.getElementById('demo-numbers').hidden = !e.target.checked;
});
</script>
</DocsLayout>
